  "title": "National Grid Seeks to Freeze Gas Delivery Rates for Customers in New York City and on Long Island",
  "summary": "National Grid today filed a Rate Stabilization Proposal with the New York State Public Service Commission (PSC) to freeze gas delivery rates for the company’s 1.9 million customers in New York City and on Long Island. If approved, rates for gas customers approved under the current rate plan would remain in effect for one additional year, from April 1, 2027, to March 31, 2028.",
